00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.920
Tesla posted its strongest second-quarter results to date.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:33.900
Record quarterly deliveries came from a refreshed Model Y, higher oil prices, and US incentives.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.520
European registrations surged in the run-up to the delivery report.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.220
Germany saw volumes quadruple a year over year to more than 16,000 units.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.660
The United Kingdom reached 30% electric vehicle share in June.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.340
Tesla's own UK volumes rose 42% month over month.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.540
That momentum now sets the baseline for second half production planning.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:04.040
With Europe now contributing more volume, look at how Tesla plans to scale one of its key plants there.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.620
Tesla revised its outlook for Gigaburlin upward.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.760
The plant is now targeted at an annual capacity of 400,000 vehicles.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.040
Earlier comments had downplayed near-term expansion at the site.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.900
Improved Model Y availability and stronger European demand signals drove the change.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.820
Berlin is positioned to become a larger share of total output alongside Texas and Shanghai.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:35.820
While Berlin scales hardware, Tesla is also pushing software capability to a much larger installed base.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:42.600
Tesla began rolling out a lighter version of full-self driving to roughly 4 million older vehicles.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.360
These cars were built before the current hardware generation.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.900
The update delivers core autonomy features through over-the-air delivery.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.320
No hardware changes are required for owners of these earlier models.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:02.640
The move expands the fleet running FSD while newer hardware remains the focus for unsupervised work.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.900
As more cars gain autonomy features, Tesla is also extending financial services tied to those same vehicles.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.200
Tesla insurance will launch in Washington State in the coming weeks.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.560
The product uses real-time vehicle data to set premiums.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.540
Washington becomes the latest addition after earlier state rollouts.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:28.120
